-- title:
--   Blow-up chart C[J/a] under flat adically dense base change
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $K$ a field with an $A$-algebra structure, and $C \subseteq K$ an $A$-subalgebra. Fix a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$, an ideal $J$ of $C$, and $a \in J$ whose image in $K$ is non-zero. Let $B_a$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by restriction of scalars from the $C$-subalgebra generated by $\{x \in K : \exists i \in J,\ x a = i\}$, i.e. the affine blow-up chart $C[J/a]$, and let $P$ be a maximal ideal of $B_a$ such that for every $b \in C$ whose image lies in $B_a$ one has $b \in P$ exactly when $b \in y$. Let $S$ be a commutative ring and $\Psi \colon C \to S$ a ring homomorphism making $S$ a flat $C$-module, put $\mathfrak n = \Psi(y)S$ and $\mathfrak M = \Psi(J)S$, and assume that for every $n$ and every $s \in S$ there is $c \in C$ with $\Psi c - s \in \mathfrak n^n$, and that $\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak n^n) = y^n$ for all $n$. Write $L_a$ for the localisation of $S$ away from $\Psi a$ and $R \subseteq L_a$ for the subring generated by the image of $S$ together with $\{x : \exists i \in \mathfrak M,\ x \cdot \Psi a = i\}$. Then $\Psi a$ is a non-zero-divisor of $S$ and lies in $\mathfrak M$; there is a ring homomorphism $\Phi \colon B_a \to L_a$ taking values in $R$, agreeing with $\Psi$ on elements of $C$ that lie in $B_a$, and satisfying $\Phi(x) \cdot \Psi a = \Psi(i)$ whenever $x \in B_a$, $i \in J$ and $x a = i$; and there is a maximal ideal $P'$ of $R$ such that $\Phi(b) \in P'$ exactly when $b \in P$, such that every $s \in \mathfrak n$ whose image lies in $R$ lies in $P'$, and such that there is a ring isomorphism $T \colon \widehat{(B_a)}_P \to \widehat{R}_{P'}$ of the $P$-adic and $P'$-adic completions with $T(\hat b) = \widehat{\Phi b}$ for all $b \in B_a$.
--
--   This is the statement that the affine blow-up chart $C[J/a]$ commutes with a flat base change $\Psi \colon C \to S$ that is adically dense at $y$ with the expected kernels, together with the resulting identification of the completions at the corresponding closed points; the proof cites the flat base-change description of the adjoined-quotients algebra ([`Algebra.adjoin_div_tensorProduct_bijective_of_flat`](thm.html#Algebra.adjoin_div_tensorProduct_bijective_of_flat)) and the criterion for an isomorphism of adic completions from levelwise surjectivity and kernel computations ([`AdicCompletion.exists_ringEquiv_of_forall_quotient_mk_comp_surjective_of_forall_ker_eq_pow`](thm.html#AdicCompletion.exists_ringEquiv_of_forall_quotient_mk_comp_surjective_of_forall_ker_eq_pow)). It is used to transfer blow-up charts of modular curves at full level to local charts, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_localChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_localChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_localChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_blowupChartAt_localChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked).
